course: dictionary
lesson: 2083
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around the word, because they are its context. «The consultant told the bakery how to sell more cakes.» Here a consultant is a person who gives expert advice, because the bakery is asking for help.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another setting. «The consultant checked the patient's heart and wrote a note.» Patient and heart are clues that this is a hospital, so a consultant here is a senior doctor who is an expert in one area.
explain: The phrase «on the bench» means a consultant has no project to work on right now. Whenever you meet a word with more than one meaning, swap each meaning into the sentence and choose the one that still makes sense.
fact: A consultant is a person whose job is to give expert advice to businesses or people.
fact: In UK and Irish hospitals, a consultant is a senior doctor who is an expert in one area, such as a heart consultant.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so always check the context before you decide.
fact: «On the bench» means a consultant has no project to work on right now.
fact: In some maths problems, a consultant charges a set amount for each hour of work.
exercise: «The consultant told the bakery how to sell more cakes.» What is a consultant here? | *A person who gives expert advice | A child who sells cakes | A cake that is sold in shops | A baker who makes bread
exercise: «The consultant checked the patient's heart and wrote a note.» In a hospital, what is a consultant? | *A senior doctor who is an expert in one area | A teacher who writes notes | A nurse who cleans the rooms | A patient waiting for a bed
exercise: «Sam is a computer consultant who helps companies.» What does a computer consultant do? | Sells computers in a shop | *Gives expert advice on computers | Fixes roads | Plays games for money
test: «The business consultant was on the bench, so she had no project to work on.» What does «on the bench» mean? | She was being paid to rest | She was sitting on a park bench | *She had no project to work on right now | She had won a prize
test: In a UK hospital, a consultant is best described as | A new patient who has just arrived | A nurse on the night shift | *A senior doctor who is an expert in one area | A person who cleans the hospital
exam: «The consultant charges per hour, so a two-hour visit costs twice as much as a one-hour visit.» What does consultant mean in this sentence? | A doctor who works in a hospital | A sort of clock | A type of cake | *A person hired to give expert advice
